Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.

Context: None

Question: Calculate the electrostatic energy of a system consisting of a point charge q located at the center of a spherical conducting shell of inner radius r_1 and outer radius r_2.

Options: 
A. {{1 / (4\pi\epsilon_0)}} (q / r^2)
B. {{1 / (4\pi\epsilon_0)}} (1/4) q^2 {{(1 / r_1) - (1 / r_2)}}
C. {{1 / (4\pi\epsilon_0)}} (q / r_1) - (q / r_2)
D. {{1 / (4\pi\epsilon_0)}} (1/2) q^2 {{(1 / r_1) - (1 / r_2)}}
E. {{1 / (4\pi\epsilon_0)}} (1/2) q^2 {{(1 / r^2) - (1 / r_1)}}
F. {{1 / (4\pi\epsilon_0)}} q^2 {{(r_2 - r_1) / (r_1 r_2)}}
G. {{1 / (4\pi\epsilon_0)}} (q^2 / r_1)
H. {{1 / (4\pi\epsilon_0)}} (q^2 / r_2)
I. {{1 / (4\pi\epsilon_0)}} (q^2 / r_1) - (q^2 / r_2)
J. {{1 / (4\pi\epsilon_0)}} (1/2) q^2 {{(1 / r_1) + (1 / r_2)}}

Provide the correct letter choice in \boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.
